                <td width=572 valign=center colspan=10 style="width:343.6000pt;padding:0.0000pt 5.4000pt 0.0000pt 5.4000pt ;border-left:none;
mso-border-left-alt:none;border-right:1.0000pt solid windowtext;mso-border-right-alt:0.5000pt solid windowtext;
border-top:none;mso-border-top-alt:0.5000pt solid windowtext;border-bottom:1.0000pt solid windowtext;
mso-border-bottom-alt:0.5000pt solid windowtext;">
                    <p class=MsoNormal><span style="font-family:仿宋;mso-bidi-font-family:'Times New Roman';font-size:12.0000pt;
mso-font-kerning:1.0000pt;"><font face="仿宋"><p>Oral and maxillofacial surgery is a discipline focused on surgical treatment, specializing in the prevention and management of diseases affecting oral organs (teeth, alveolar bone, lips, cheeks, tongue, palate, pharynx), facial soft tissues, maxillofacial bones (maxilla, mandible, zygomatic bone), temporomandibular joint, salivary glands, and specific neck conditions. The curriculum structure, as outlined in the "Oral and Maxillofacial Surgery" syllabus, comprises three core components: theoretical instruction, laboratory courses, and clinical practice. This syllabus specifically addresses the clinical practice component.</p></font></span><span style="font-family:'Times New Roman';mso-fareast-font-family:仿宋;font-size:10.5000pt;
mso-font-kerning:1.0000pt;"><o:p></o:p></span></p>
                </td>
            </tr>
            <tr style="height:19.9000pt;">
                <td width=777 valign=center colspan=14 style="width:466.7000pt;padding:0.0000pt 5.4000pt 0.0000pt 5.4000pt ;border-left:1.0000pt solid windowtext;
